{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"0a8bb689e05cfd93534b89136f0c1a8d364980ec0860134bc2ef67b4632665c4","packTokens":3071,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":203,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":497,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":2219,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"failures","tokens":40,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's PostgreSQL database (the connection string named App, which the project already reads).\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"No test may count on those rows, because the app runs that file only when Seed:Demo is true.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Do not build screens here; the web app is built in its own repo.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Should implementation be limited to behavior explicitly defined in contracts/openapi.yaml, or should it also implement narrative-only parking rules and external workflows (such as release/claim timing, notifications, camera integration, and weekly email reporting)?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Implement only the operations and behavior explicitly defined in contracts/openapi.yaml; leave narrative-only behavior and integrations out.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"For application tables that have no sample record in the contract's examples, how should SeedData.cs satisfy the request for sample rows in each table?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Create a few plausible, schema-valid rows for those tables, using contract example values wherever available.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"What source should provide the Google Workspace OAuth client ID, client secret, and redirect URI needed to implement the contract's Google authorization operation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Read these values from deployment configuration or secrets, with values supplied for each environment.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What should implementation assume about the existing App database when adding the tables required by the API?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat App as a fresh/empty database and use the existing EnsureCreated startup behavior; no migration or backfill is required.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"This spec contains 27 requirements—about three runs’ worth of work. Should it be approved as one run, or should it be narrowed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Approve the full spec as one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement `GET /api/auth/google/authorization` from the OpenAPI contract, using deployment-configured Google OAuth values to return an authorization URL and non-empty state, or the contract-defined 503 error when configuration or the authorization service is unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Implement `POST /api/auth/sign-in` to exchange the authorization code and state with Google using configured OAuth values, accept only eligible Folio3 Workspace identities, return the contracted session fields, and return the contract-defined 400, 401, or 503 errors for invalid requests, unaccepted identities, or unavailable Google service.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `GET /api/employees/me` to return the employee's contract-required profile and vehicles, with contract-defined 401, 403, or 404 errors for absent or invalid authentication, insufficient access, or a missing profile.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `GET /api/parking/dashboard` to return the contracted dashboard fields for an identified employee, with a contract-defined 401 error when authentication is invalid.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `POST /api/parking/releases/today` to release eligible dedicated parking for today in the office timezone, return the release and its audit event, and use contract-defined 401, 403, or 409 errors as applicable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `GET /api/vehicles` to list only the authenticated employee's vehicles using the contract fields, with a contract-defined 401 error when authentication is invalid.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `POST /api/vehicles` to register a vehicle for the employee and return it as active, with contract-defined 400, 401, or 409 errors for invalid input, absent authentication, or a conflicting plate.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `GET /api/parking/releases` to return only the employee's releases and their audit events using the contract fields, with a contract-defined 401 error when authentication is invalid.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `POST /api/parking/releases` to schedule one or more releases within the next 30 calendar days for an eligible dedicated-parking holder, recording a scheduled audit event for each, and return contract-defined 400, 403, or 422 errors as applicable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `DELETE /api/parking/releases/{releaseId}` to cancel an owned, unclaimed scheduled release and return its scheduling and cancellation audit events, with contract-defined 401, 403, 404, or 409 errors as applicable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `GET /api/parking/availability` to return the contracted date, timezone, capacity, release-time, and floor availability data, with a contract-defined 401 error when authentication is invalid.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `POST /api/parking/claims` to allocate a claimable temporary space using the employee's registered vehicle, return the contracted allocation fields, and ensure concurrent attempts for the last space produce exactly one success and one 409 conflict; return applicable contract-defined errors for invalid, unauthenticated, ineligible, or unavailable claims.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `GET /api/parking/claims/today` to return the employee's active temporary allocation for today, or contract-defined 404 or 401 errors when there is no allocation or authentication is invalid.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Implement bearer-authenticated `DELETE /api/parking/claims/{claimId}` to cancel an owned claim when its state permits and return the contracted claim fields and cancellation outcome, with contract-defined 401, 403, 404, or 409 errors as applicable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Implement administrator-authorized `GET /api/admin/roster` with the documented search, assignment, and pagination parameters, contracted response, and contract-defined 401 or 403 errors for unauthenticated or non-administrator callers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Implement administrator-authorized `GET /api/admin/entry-checks` with the documented filters, contracted response, and contract-defined 401 or 403 errors for unauthenticated or non-administrator callers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Implement unauthenticated `POST /api/entrance/verify` to process car and non-car detections, report the contracted verification outcome and indicator command, record every outcome in App for later entry-check queries, and return contract-defined 400 or 503 errors for malformed requests or unavailable required services.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Implement administrator-authorized `GET /api/admin/utilization` to return the contracted weekly utilization report for an omitted or valid week start, with contract-defined 400, 401, or 403 errors for invalid dates, unauthenticated callers, or non-administrators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Implement administrator-authorized `GET /api/admin/office-settings` to return the stored contracted office parking settings, with contract-defined 401 or 403 errors for unauthenticated or non-administrator callers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Implement administrator-authorized `PUT /api/admin/office-settings` to validate and save the timezone, release time, and non-empty report recipients so subsequent reads return those values, with contract-defined 400, 401, or 403 errors as applicable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Implement administrator-authorized `GET /api/admin/activity` with the documented filters and response field `activity` as specified by the d1 reading, and contract-defined 401 or 403 errors for unauthenticated or non-administrator callers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Implement administrator-authorized `GET /api/admin/activity` with the documented filters and response field `events` and contracted activity records as specified by the d2 and d3 readings, and contract-defined 401 or 403 errors for unauthenticated or non-administrator callers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Implement unauthenticated `POST /api/notifications/availability` to dispatch the fixed `parking-availability` template through the configured email service to eligible non-dedicated employees, return a 202 dispatch response when accepted, and return contract-defined 400 or 503 errors for invalid requests or unavailable email service.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Persist API-managed application records in the PostgreSQL database configured by `ConnectionStrings:App` and initialize its schema at startup using the existing fresh-database `EnsureCreated` behavior.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"When `Seed:Demo` is true, use `App.Api/SeedData.cs` to seed schema-valid sample rows into every empty application table, with two to five rows per table, at least one valid row for any contract-defined singleton table, contract examples where available, and plausible values otherwise; expose `SeedData.Run` publicly.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"Keep demo-only sample records absent when `Seed:Demo` is unset or false, and ensure contract tests arrange their own records and identities as needed so they pass without demo-seed rows, with an empty roster containing zero employees.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"Keep the repository's product surfaces limited to contracted HTTP operations and API documentation, without employee, administrator, or security-guard product screens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"Implement all operations declared by the locked OpenAPI contract using its request, response, and security definitions.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L8 anchors] REQ-24 has an anchor that doesn't match the code\n</failures>\n\nMap the sentences."}